2412	//  P2 — EMBEDDING grad (tok/pos). dh0 [T,d] (bf16) holds grad wrt h0.
2413	//
2414	//  WAS (the owner-LINEAR-SCAN, task #13 H2 target): each of V owner-CTAs scanned
2415	//  ALL T tokens (`if tok_ids[t]==r` per token), re-reading the WHOLE dh0 stream V
2416	//  times — O(V·d·T) work + V passes over 134 MB of dh0, where O(d·T) (ONE pass)
2417	//  suffices. V=99<132 left 33 CTAs idle; threads beyond d idled per owner; pos
2418	//  used only S=4 owner-CTAs scanning all T with a t%S branch.
2419	//
2420	//  NOW (H2 — counting-sort token lists + flat-element grid-stride):
2421	//    BUILD (dectc_embed_build_lists, once, cta 0, in the P1 window so it overlaps
2422	//    fwd/bwd and adds NO barrier — B1 already fences it before P2 consumes):
2423	//    a deterministic integer counting sort over tok_ids → row_start[V+1] (CSR
2424	//    offsets) + perm[T] (token positions bucketed by vocab row, ASCENDING t
2425	//    within each row, because the scatter visits t ascending and appends).
2426	//    CONSUME (dectc_embed_owner_scan): a flat grid-stride over ALL V·d output
2427	//    elements. Element (r,j) walks ONLY row r's own tokens perm[row_start[r] ..
2428	//    row_start[r+1]) in ascending-t order, reading dh0[perm[i]·d + j]. Total
2429	//    work collapses to O(d·T) (each dh0 value read once in aggregate); reads are
2430	//    COALESCED (consecutive threads = consecutive j on the same token row); ALL
2431	//    132 CTAs + full blockDim are busy (V·d=101376 elems ≫ 132·256). pos is the
2432	//    same flat grid-stride but needs NO list: tokens with (t%S)==p are exactly
2433	//    t = p, p+S, …, p+(B-1)·S (T=B·S), a closed-form ascending walk of length B.
2434	//
2435	//  DETERMINISM: per row the accumulation order over its tokens is the SAME fixed
2436	//  ascending-t order as the old scan (perm is built ascending; pos walk is
2437	//  ascending) → bitwise-identical fp32 accumulation, no float atomics, no timing-
2438	//  dependent order. The build is integer-exact (histogram counts + prefix +
2439	//  serial ascending scatter), so row_start/perm are bit-identical every rerun.
2440	//
2441	//  PORTABLE: this CSR-bucket + flat-element grid-stride is the general pattern for
2442	//  any "gather grad into a small set of embedding/lookup rows" — vit patch-proj /
2443	//  pos-embed rows and mamba's embedding will reuse dectc_embed_build_lists +
2444	//  this consume verbatim (only the row count V and the membership map differ; a
2445	//  structural map like pos needs no list at all).
2446	// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
